WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.720
Organizations cannot govern AI systems they do not know exist.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:10.180
An AI inventory records where AI is used, what purpose it serves, what data it processes, and who owns it.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:19.920
Inventory should also capture what model, service, dataset, vendor, tool, or integration the system depends on, along with risks that require attention.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:29.820
Ownership matters because someone must be responsible for approving changes, reviewing performance, responding to incidents, and making sure the system remains appropriate for its use case.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:34.680
Visibility turns AI governance from an abstract idea into an operating practice.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.820
It gives teams a common place to see what exists and who is accountable.
